  "raw": {
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/31928": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Animal Medicine",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Animal Medicine Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Animal Medicine Position ID: UMASSMED-PathAnimalMed-RAP [#31928] Position Title: Assistant Professor Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Veterinary Medicine / Laboratory Animal Medicine Appl Deadline: 2026/11/30 23:59:59  (posted 2026/04/08 , listed until 2026/11/30) Position Description: Apply Position Description Clinical Veterinarian, Assistant/Associate Professor, Non-Tenure Track\r\nDepartment of Animal Medicine The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School and the Department of Animal Medicine invite applications for a Non-Tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor Level, depending on experience and qualifications, for a Clinical Veterinarian. The Clinical Veterinarian is responsible for providing and overseeing veterinary medical and surgical care for all research animals on campus. Specific responsibilities will be and not limited to, oversight of veterinary technicians, IACUC policy and protocol reviews, consultations with investigators regarding IACUC, clinical and research related issues, and oversight of the animal enrichment program. Required qualifications include DVM/VMD from AVMA approved College of Veterinary Medicine or equivalent. Eligible for or have a valid license to practice Veterinary Medicine in MA. If eligible, obtain an MA license within 3 months of hire. USDA category II accreditation in MA or obtain accreditation within 1.5 years of hire. \r\nACLAM board certification or eligibility, if eligible the applicant must achieve ACLAM board certification within 18 months of appointment. Private practice or rotating internship experience, ABSL3 experience, or a graduate degree in biomedical science are preferred qualifications. Computer, communication, and organizational skills, regulatory knowledge, and the ability to work independently in a diverse environment are key competencies for the position. This position is considered essential, and as such requires weekend, holiday, off-hours and inclement weather coverage as needed on a rotating basis.\r\nApplications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a curriculum vita, cover letter, contact information for four references, and a statement on diversity, equity and inclusion to: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/31928 .\r\n \r\nUMass Chan Medical School is committed to being an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer and recognizes the power of a diverse community. We encourage applications from protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and those with varied experiences, perspectives and backgrounds to consider UMass Chan Medical School as their employer of choice. Hiring Range: $108,438 (minimum) $172,381 (maximum) In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the base salary range for this\r\nposition is listed above (exclusive of benefits and retirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a combination of factors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also consider internal equity to ensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position. Offers are typically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and development within the role. In addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement plan. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Publication list DEI Statement And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://inside.umassmed.edu/AnimalMedicine/ UMASS Medical School Department of Animal Medicine 55 Lake Ave North Worcester, MA  01655-0002 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/27680": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, Corrigan Mental Health Center - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-APCORRIGAN [#27680, 24-072] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, Corrigan Mental Health Center Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Fall River, Massachusetts 02720, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: (posted 2024/05/23 , listed until 2027/04/12) Position Description: Apply Position Description CORRIGAN MENTAL HEALTH CENTER ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a board-certified or board-\r\neligible adult psychiatrist to serve as an Attending Psychiatrist for a Department of Mental Health \r\noperated mental health center in Fall River, MA. The facility is composed of a 16-bed, inpatient psychiatric unit, partial hospital program, outpatient services, and community services. Candidates interested in either full-time or part-time work will be considered. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or Associate Professor based on qualifications. The Attending Psychiatrist is responsible for providing direct clinical care to adult patients \r\nunder the supervision of the Facility Medical Director. The Attending Psychiatrist is a part of a \r\nmulti-disciplinary team and participates in regular clinical and risk consultation meetings, as well as quality and performance improvement initiatives. We seek an inspired clinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will \r\npossess both a depth and breadth of adult psychiatric experience and commitment to public sector psychiatry. Benefits: \r\n- A generous benefit plan by UMass Chan \r\n- The option to enroll in either the Massachusetts State Retirement Board pension scheme (defined benefit) or the ORP (defined contribution plan). \r\n- Holidays, paid time off, educational days, sick days, and vacation totaling more than 8 weeks. \r\n- Annual professional education stipend. \r\n- UMass-sponsored J1- Conrad waiver / H1b visa and Green Card applications. \r\n- DMH-sponsored student loan repayment program for providers of direct care in any of the DMH state-operated facilities, in exchange for four (4) years of dedicated service. This position is eligible for DMH loan repayment. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department, University and \r\nDMH. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity, and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching, and scholarship. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a\r\ndiverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, \r\nperspectives, and backgrounds.\r\nFor additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry please view our \r\nwebsite at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ For questions about this position, please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair for Public Sector \r\nPsychiatry at bdaly@communityhealthlink.org Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ Department of Psychiatry UMass Chan Medical School 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
