    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32836": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, Taunton State Hospital - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-ATTPSYCH [#32836, 27-019] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, Taunton State Hospital Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/09/24 , listed until 2027/08/04) Position Description: Apply Position Description TAUNTON STATE HOSPITAL, INPATIENT ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a board-certified or\r\nboard-eligible adult psychiatrist to serve as an Inpatient Attending Psychiatrist for the Department\r\nof Mental Health(DMH) operated inpatient psychiatric units at Taunton State Hospital in Taunton,\r\nMA. The units are composed of 60 adult psychiatric beds serving persons in need of forensic\r\nevaluation and continuing inpatient care. The Inpatient Attending Psychiatrist is responsible for providing direct clinical care to adult\r\ninpatients under the supervision of the Facility Medical Director. The Inpatient Attending\r\nPsychiatrist is a part of a multi-disciplinary team and participates in regular clinical and risk\r\nconsultation meetings, as well as quality and performance improvement initiatives. We seek an inspired clinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will\r\npossess both a depth and breadth of adult psychiatric experience and commitment to public sector\r\npsychiatry. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as\r\nAssistant or Associate Professor based on qualifications. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or\r\nAssociate Professor based on qualifications. which includes Departmental support for clinical,\r\ntraining and research. The faculty benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for professional\r\ndevelopment totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance;\r\neligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a defined contribution\r\nretirement plan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for voluntary night,\r\nweekends, and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement. The UMass Chan Medical School welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and\r\nfederal anti-discrimination laws. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental\r\nHealth base salary for board certified applicants is $247,000.00 (exclusive of benefits and\r\nretirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a combination of factors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also consider internal equity to ensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position. Offers are typically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and development within the role. In addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which\r\nincludes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement\r\nplan. *Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University.\r\nAccordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute\r\nto racial equity, diversity and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching and scholarship. *\r\nAs an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value\r\nof a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences,\r\nperspectives, and backgrounds. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA  01655 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29778": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, WRCH - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-ATTPSYCHWRCH3 [#29778, 25045] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, WRCH Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: none  (listed until 2027/04/12) Position Description: Apply Position Description ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST POSITION WORCESTER RECOVERY CENTER AND HOSPITAL\r\n\r\nWORCESTER RECOVERY CENTER AND HOSPITAL and the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences at the University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a full-time (40 hours per week) board-certified/board-eligible psychiatrist to serve at the Worcester Recovery Center and Hospital in Worcester, MA. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or Associate Professor based on qualifications. Academic Opportunities: Provide supervision to psychiatry fellows, psychiatry residents, and medical students. Access departmental support for leadership development, research, and other academic pursuits through various UMass Chan–sponsored programs. Participate in a variety of continuing medical education (CME) activities, including grand rounds, journal clubs, law and psychiatry lectures, and DMH-sponsored training courses, workshops, and events. We seek an inspired clinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will possess both a depth and breadth of adult psychiatric experience and commitment to public sector psychiatry. Major Responsibilities Provide direct clinical care to adult patients under the supervision of the Facility Medical Director. Collaborate as part of a multidisciplinary team and participate in regular clinical and risk consultation meetings, as well as quality and performance improvement initiatives. Be responsible for the admission and discharge of patients who meet appropriate DMH criteria. Be assigned to a unit by the Facility Medical Director and assume overall responsibility for the care of patients on the assigned treatment team. This includes ensuring each patient receives a comprehensive assessment, accurate diagnostic formulation, appropriate problem list, and an interdisciplinary treatment plan, along with ongoing monitoring, evaluation, consultation, and collaboration as needed to ensure patient safety and appropriate care. Lead the assigned Treatment Team and delegate responsibilities to team members in alignment with their disciplines and the goals of the treatment plan. Required Qualifications Board-certified or board- eligible adult psychiatrist Preferred Qualifications We seek an inspired clinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will possess a depth and breadth of adult psychiatric experience and demonstrated ability to function as a clinical leader in a multidisciplinary environment. Additional Data Benefits: A generous benefit plan by UMass Chan - The option to enroll in either the Massachusetts State Retirement Board pension scheme (defined benefit) or the ORP (defined contribution plan). Holidays, paid time off, educational days, sick days, and vacation totaling more than 8 weeks. Annual professional education stipend. UMass-sponsored J1- Conrad waiver / H1b visa and Green Card applications. DMH-sponsored student loan repayment program for providers of direct care in any of the DMH state-operated facilities, in exchange for four (4) years of dedicated service. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental Health base salary for this position is $255,000 (exclusive of benefits and retirement). Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department, University and DMH. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity, and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching, and scholarship. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. For additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry please view our website at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ For questions about this position, please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair for Public Sector Psychiatry at brian.daly@umassmed.edu. UMass Chan welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/dop/ 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29511": {
      "title": "Child and Adolescent Attending Psychiatrist - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-CHILDPSYCHWRCH [#29511, 25038] Position Title: Child and Adolescent Attending Psychiatrist Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: none  (listed until 2027/04/12) Position Description: Apply Position Description INPATIENT CHILD AND ADOLESCENT ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST, ADOLESCENT CONTINUING CARE UNITS\r\nWORCESTER RECOVERY CENTER AND HOSPITAL The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) is seeking a full-time (40 hours \r\nper-week) board-certified/board-eligible child and adolescent psychiatrist to serve the Adolescent \r\nContinuing Care Unit (ACCU) at the Worcester Recovery Center and Hospital (WRCH) in Worcester, MA. WRCH is a Department of Mental Health (DMH) state-of-the-art hospital that cares for adults and adolescents and their families with severe mental health conditions. The ACCU is both part of WRCH and the statewide Department of Mental Health Child, Youth, and Families (CYF) Services. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or Associate Professor based on qualifications. The Attending Child and Adolescent psychiatrist will provide comprehensive psychiatric care to \r\nadolescents admitted to the ACCU. This care includes: * treatment planning for adolescents with complex mental health conditions at risk of or\r\ndemonstrating self-harm or harm to others; * individualized, strength-based, trauma-informed, and trauma-responsive psychiatric care; * care that supports recovery and collaborates with the youth and their legally authorized representative(s)/families, as well as appropriate collateral care team members, to ensure\r\ntreatment is active and moves the youth toward the least restrictive environment as soon as\r\npossible; and, * psychiatry/psychopharmacology services that accord with current best practices for adolescents\r\nand are informed by evidence-based practices. As indicated, the attending child and adolescent psychiatrist also participates in forensic \r\nevaluations and testifies in court for youth admitted to the unit on forensic legal statuses (evaluation of competency, criminal responsibility, etc.). The ACCU is a family-friendly work environment, with no required nights or weekend calls. There are opportunities to join the on-call team for additional moonlighting with competitive reimbursement. Academic Opportunities: \r\n- Supervision of child and adolescent psychiatry fellows, psychiatry residents and medical students. \r\n- Opportunity to be involved in the Child and Adolescent Psychiatry Fellowship. \r\n- Department support for leadership training, research, and other academic endeavors through various \r\nUMass Chan-sponsored programs. \r\n- Various CME activities, including grand rounds, journal clubs, law and psychiatry lectures, and DMH-sponsored trainings, workshops and events. Benefits: - A generous benefit plan by UMass Chan - The option to enroll in either the \r\nMassachusetts State Retirement Board pension scheme (defined benefit) or the ORP (defined contribution plan). - Holidays, paid time off, educational days, sick days, and vacation totaling more than 8 weeks. - Annual professional education stipend. - UMass-sponsored J1- Conrad waiver / H1b visa and Green Card applications. - DMH-sponsored student loan repayment program for providers of direct care in any of the DMH state-operated facilities, in exchange for four (4) years of dedicated service. This position is eligible for state-sponsored loan repayment. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department, University and \r\nDMH. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity, and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching, and scholarship. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. For additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry please view our website at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ ; For questions about this position, please contact Yael Dvir, Vice Chair, Child and Adolescent Psychiatry Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/21875": {
      "title": "Facility Medical Director, Pocasset, MA - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-FMDPOC [#21875, 22-110] Position Title: Facility Medical Director, Pocasset, MA Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: none  (listed until 2026/10/18) Position Description: Apply Position Description POCASSET FACILITY MEDICAL DIRECTOR The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a board-certified psychiatrist to serve as the Facility Medical Director (FMD) for The Cape Cod and the Islands Community Mental Health Center in Pocasset, MA. Successful candidates will receive a faculty appointment that includes Department of Psychiatry support for clinical, training and research. There is the option for voluntary night, weekend and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement. Major Responsibilities Serve as the Facility Medical Director (FMD) for The Cape Cod and Islands Community Mental Health Center, acting as the chief physician and clinical leader for both inpatient and partial hospitalization programs. Oversee the delivery of high-quality clinical care and treatment across all services. Lead the development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of all clinical programs within the Center. Ensure the maintenance of professional practice standards, including staff composition, performance evaluation, education, and ongoing training. Direct the recruitment, scheduling, and supervision of psychiatrists and advanced practice nurses assigned through this contract, including UMass Chan Medical School clinicians, credentialed per diem providers, and locum tenens staff. Provide medical leadership to ensure compliance with CMS, Joint Commission, DMH, and DPH standards, and support preparation for all licensure and accreditation reviews. Collaborate with DMH service providers and contracted agencies, offering clinical consultation as appropriate. Oversee key operational areas including utilization management, risk management, support of DMH initiatives, and clinical and psychopharmacology services. Participate in research activities, with opportunities for protected time based on experience and organizational goals. Required Qualifications Board-certified Psychiatrist Additional Data This position is eligible for a hybrid/remote schedule combining regularly scheduled on-site time at the facility in Pocasset, MA, and remote/virtual coverage. Benefits: Access to comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance. Enroll in either the Massachusetts State Retirement Board pension scheme (defined benefit) or the ORP (defined contribution plan). 14 paid holidays annually, vacation and sick time, and educational days, totaling more than 8 weeks. Annual professional education stipend. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental Health base salary for this position is $300,000 (exclusive of benefits and retirement). UMass-sponsored J1- Conrad waiver / H1b visa and Green Card applications. This position qualifies for the DMH loan repayment program. In addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement plan Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity, and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching, and scholarship. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. For additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry please view our website at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ ; For questions about this position, please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair, Public Sector Psychiatry (brian.daly@umassmed.edu). UMass Chan welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry UMass Chan Medical School 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/31724": {
      "title": "Forensic Psychiatrist, Worcester Recovery Center and Hospital - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-FORENSICPSYCH [#31724, 26037] Position Title: Forensic Psychiatrist, Worcester Recovery Center and Hospital Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/02/23 , listed until 2027/02/28) Position Description: Apply Position Description Forensic Psychiatrist WRCH WORCESTER RECOVERY CENTER AND HOSPITAL (WRCH), a Department of Mental Health (DMH) hospital, and the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences at the University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) is seeking a full-time (40 hours per week) board-certified or board-eligible (forensic) psychiatrist to serve on one of the court-evaluation units (CEUs). WRCH is the largest psychiatric facility in MA, a state-of-the-art hospital built in 2012, serving individuals with severe mental health conditions from across the state. While forensic training is recommended, it is not required for interested psychiatrists to apply. The hospital offers ongoing trainings and strong academic, administrative, and legal supports for all providers and staff. Academic Opportunities: Supervision of psychiatry residents and medical students; Department support for leadership training, research, and other educational endeavors through various UMass Chan-sponsored programs; Various CME activities, including grand rounds, journal clubs, law and psychiatry lectures, and DMH-sponsored trainings, workshops and events. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or Associate Professor based on qualifications. which includes Departmental support for clinical, training and research. The benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for professional development totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance; eligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a defined contribution retirement plan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for voluntary night, weekends, and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement. The UMass Chan Medical School welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental Health base salary for this position is $255,000 (exclusive of benefits and retirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a combination of factors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also consider internal equity to ensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position. Offers are typically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and development within the role. In addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement plan *Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching and scholarship. *\r\nAs an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. For additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry, please view our website at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ For questions about this position this position, please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair, Public Sector Psychiatry (brian.daly@umassmemorial.org) or Margarita Abi Zeid Daou, MD, Associate Facility Medical Director, WRCH (margarita.abizeiddaou@umassmed.edu). Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA  01655 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32568": {
      "title": "Mobile Forensic Psychologist - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-FORENSICPSYCH1 [#32568, 27010-27013] Position Title: Mobile Forensic Psychologist Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/09/01 , listed until 2027/03/01) Position Description: Apply Position Description Four Open Positions Available! Mobile Forensic Psychologist UMass Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry & Behavioral Sciences The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School Department of Psychiatry & Behavioral Sciences Law and Psychiatry program seeks to fill four full-time 1.0 FTE Faculty positions on its Mobile Forensic Evaluation Service. The Service provides forensic evaluations of competence to stand trial, criminal responsibility, civil commitment, and aid-in sentencing at the Worcester Recovery Center and Hospital, Tewksbury State Hospital and Mountain View Unit at Valley Springs Behavioral Healthcare. In addition, the Service provides violence risk assessment consultations to Department of Mental Health Facilities. The successful candidate will have a Ph.D./Psy.D., specialized training/experience in Forensic Psychology, have experience in risk assessment, and be licensed or eligible for licensure as a psychologist in Massachusetts. In addition, the successful candidate will demonstrate ability to contribute to the academic mission of UMass Chan Medical School, including within our Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program and/or Psychology Internship Program. The position is open to early career forensic psychologists and those with more experience. Depending on experience, there are opportunities for leadership positions within the program as well as in the associated Forensic Residency Program. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant Professor based on qualifications. The position offers competitive salaries, with an excellent benefit package, including additional faculty benefits. The benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for professional development totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance; eligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a defined contribution retirement plan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for voluntary night, weekends, and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement. The UMass Chan Medical School welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental Health base salary for this position is $124,793.75 (exclusive of benefits and retirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a combination of factors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also consider internal equity to ensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position. Offers are typically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and development within the role.\r\nIn addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement plan *Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to racial equity, diversity and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching and scholarship.* As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. Information about our Law and Psychiatry program is available at: https://www.umassmed.edu/lawandpsychiatry/ The University of Massachusetts (Campus) welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA  01655 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/24877": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, Brockton - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-PSYCHIATRISTBROCKTONFT [#24877, 23090] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, Brockton Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Brockton, Massachusetts 02302, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: none  (listed until 2026/10/18) Position Description: Apply Position Description BROCKTON MULTI-SERVICE CENTER ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a board-eligible or board-certified adult psychiatrist to serve as a full-time Attending Psychiatrist for the Brockton \r\nMulti-Service Center (BMSC) in Brockton, MA. Clinical services located at the site include an \r\noutpatient behavioral health and medication management clinic, Adult Community Clinical Services \r\n(ACCS), Program of Assertive Community Treatment (PACT), and DMH case management services. The Attending Psychiatrist will provide outpatient clinical services to a diverse group of adult DMH \r\nclients who live in the community and in supported group living environments. We seek an inspired \r\nclinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will possess a depth and \r\nbreadth of adult psychiatric experience and demonstrated ability to function as a clinical leader in a multidisciplinary environment. \r\n\r\nSuccessful candidates will receive a faculty appointment that includes Departmental support for \r\nclinical, training and research. The benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for \r\nprofessional development totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance; eligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a \r\ndefined contribution retirement plan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for \r\nvoluntary night, weekend, and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement. This position is eligible for DMH loan repayment. J-1 and H-1B candidates are welcome and encouraged to apply. The Massachusetts Department of \r\nMental Health participates in the J-1 Waiver Program for positions, like the Attending Psychiatrist, \r\nhired into state operated programs. For additional information about the Department of Psychiatry you can view our web site \r\nat https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry For questions about this position please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair, Public Sector \r\nPsychiatry at bdaly@communityhealthlink.org. Diversity, equity and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University. \r\nAccordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified diverse candidates.\r\n\r\nAs an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value \r\nof a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, \r\nperspectives, and backgrounds Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/24869": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, Brockton Multi-Service Center - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-PSYCHIATRISTBROCKTONPT [#24869, 23086] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, Brockton Multi-Service Center Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: none  (listed until 2026/10/18) Position Description: Apply Position Description BROCKTON MULTI-SERVICE CENTER: PART-TIME ATTENDING PSYCHIATRIST The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) seeks a board-eligible or board-certified adult psychiatrist to serve as a part-time Attending Psychiatrist for The Brockton Multi-Service Center (BMSC) in Brockton, MA. Clinical services located at the site include an outpatient behavioral health and medication management clinic, Adult Community Clinical Services (ACCS), Program of Assertive Community Treatment (PACT), and DMH case management services. The Attending Psychiatrist will provide outpatient clinical services to a diverse group of adult DMH clients who live in the community and in supported group living environments. We seek an inspired clinician, committed to the recovery model of care. Ideal candidates will possess a depth and breadth of adult psychiatric experience and demonstrated ability to function as a clinical leader in a multidisciplinary environment.\r\n \r\nSuccessful candidates will receive a faculty appointment that includes Departmental support for clinical, training and research. The benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for professional development totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance; eligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a defined contribution retirement plan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for voluntary night, weekend, and holiday coverage with highly competitive reimbursement.  This position is eligible for DMH loan repayment. J-1 and H-1B candidates are welcome and encouraged to apply. The Massachusetts Department of Mental Health participates in the J-1 Waiver Program for positions, like the Attending Psychiatrist, hired into state operated programs. For additional information about the Department of Psychiatry you can view our web site at https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry For questions about this position please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair, Public Sector Psychiatry at bdaly@communityhealthlink.org. Diversity, equity and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University. Accordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified diverse candidates.\r\n\r\nAs an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry UMass Chan Medical School 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA 01605 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
