    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32421": {
      "title": "Attending Psychiatrist, WRCH - Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Department of Psychiatry Position ID: UMASSMED-Psych-PSYCHWRCH [#32421, 27-004] Position Title: Attending Psychiatrist, WRCH Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Psychiatry Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/08/06 , listed until 2027/08/04) Position Description: Apply Position Description Attending Psychiatrist, WRCH WORCESTER RECOVERY CENTER AND HOSPITAL (WRCH), a Department of Mental Health (DMH) hospital, and the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences at the University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School (UMass Chan) is seeking a full-time (40 hours per week) board-certified or board eligible psychiatrist to serve on one of the court-evaluation units (CEUs). WRCH is the largest psychiatric\r\nfacility in MA, a state-of-the-art hospital built in 2012, serving individuals with severe mental health conditions from across the state. While forensic training is recommended, it is not required for interested psychiatrists to apply. The hospital offers ongoing trainings and strong academic,\r\nadministrative, and legal supports for all providers and staff. Academic Opportunities: Supervision of psychiatry residents and medical students; Department support\r\nfor leadership training, research, and other educational endeavors through various UMass Chan sponsored\r\nprograms; Various CME activities, including grand rounds, journal clubs, law and psychiatry\r\nlectures, and DMH-sponsored trainings, workshops and events. The selected candidate will be recommended for a UMass Chan faculty appointment as Assistant or\r\nAssociate Professor based on qualifications. which includes Departmental support for clinical, training\r\nand research. The benefit package includes generous holiday and paid time off for professional\r\ndevelopment totaling to more than 7 weeks; generous medical, dental, and malpractice insurance;\r\neligibility to participate in the state’s defined benefit pension plan or a defined contribution retirement\r\nplan; and an annual practice allowance. There is the option for voluntary night, weekends, and holiday\r\ncoverage with highly competitive reimbursement. The UMass Chan Medical School welcomes all\r\nqualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the established Department of Mental Health\r\nbase salary for this position is $255,000 (exclusive of benefits and retirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a combination of\r\nfactors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also consider internal equity to\r\nensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position. Offers are\r\ntypically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and development within the role.\r\nIn addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes paid\r\ntime off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a 401A retirement plan. *Diversity, equity, and inclusion are integral to the commitment of the Department and University.\r\nAccordingly, the Department encourages applications from qualified candidates who can contribute to\r\nracial equity, diversity and inclusion through service, mentorship, teaching and scholarship. *As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a\r\ndiverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives,\r\nand backgrounds. For additional information about our mission-driven Department of Psychiatry, please view our website\r\nat https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry/hiring-mission/non-facultypositions/ For questions about this position, please contact Brian Daly, MD, Vice Chair, Public Sector Psychiatry (brian.daly@umassmemorial.org) or Margarita Abi Zeid Daou, MD, Associate Facility Medical Director, WRCH (margarita.abizeiddaou@umassmed.edu) Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.umassmed.edu/psychiatry Department of Psychiatry 55 Lake Avenue North Worcester, MA  01655 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32809": {
      "title": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Graduate School Of Nursing",
      "description": "University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Graduate School Of Nursing Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School, Graduate School Of Nursing Program ID: UMASSMED-GSN-ASSOCIATEDEAN [#32809] Program Title: Associate Dean for Advanced Practice and Leadership Programs Program Type: Non tenure-track faculty Location: Worcester, Massachusetts 01655, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Education / nursing Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/09/23 , listed until 2027/03/23) Description: Apply Description The University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School Tan Chingfen Graduate School of Nursing invites applications for a full-time, 12-month Associate Dean for Advanced Practice and Leadership Programs reporting to the Dean of the Tan Chingfen Graduate School of Nursing. This position provides leadership for the curriculum, faculty, students, and evaluation of the Advanced Practice and Leadership Programs. The Tan Chingfen Graduate School of Nursing is part of UMass Chan Medical School’s academic health science center and is dedicated to preparing nurse scientists, advanced practice nurses, nurse educators, and nurse leaders who improve health care in Massachusetts and beyond. Key Responsibilities\r\n•\tCollaborate with executive leadership to provide leadership, administrative oversight, and program development to align  with the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of the Tan Chingfen Graduate School of Nursing.\r\n•\tLead the development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of Advanced Practice and Leadership programs, ensuring compliance with accreditation standards, professional competencies, and state and national regulatory requirements.\r\n•\tCollaborate with program directors, track coordinators, faculty, and staff to support program operations, curriculum innovation, student success, and faculty excellence.\r\n•\tOversee program planning, budgeting, assessment, reporting, and quality improvement initiatives to achieve programmatic and institutional goals.\r\n•\tFoster and maintain partnerships with healthcare organizations, clinical affiliates, professional organizations, and regulatory agencies to strengthen clinical education and advance program objectives.\r\n•\tPromote student recruitment, admissions, retention, progression, and graduation through collaboration with enrollment management, student affairs, and academic leadership.\r\n•\tMentor and support faculty and academic leaders in teaching, scholarship productivity and dissemination, leadership development, and professional advancement.\r\n•\tSupport faculty and the Program Directors in addressing student academic and disciplinary concerns, which include appropriate interventions, remediation, and progression processes.\r\n•\tRepresent the Advanced Practice and Leadership Programs on School, University, and external committees, task forces, and professional organizations.\r\n•\tCollaborates with the T.H. Chan Medical School and Morning side Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences.\r\n•\tUtilize program outcome data and performance metrics to guide strategic decision-making, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement efforts.\r\n•\tMaintain a record of teaching, an active program of scholarship, and service consistent with faculty rank and institutional expectations. Required Qualifications\r\n•\tMassachusetts RN/NP licensure or eligibility for licensure. \r\n•\tDoctoral preparation (DNP or PhD) in Nursing\r\n•\tNational Certification as a Nurse Practitioner\r\n•\tA minimum of 5 years of successful administrative experience in an academic setting\r\n•\tExperience as an educator in higher education\r\n•\tRecord of scholarship commensurate with appointment at Associate or Full Professor Preferred Qualifications\r\n•\tActive clinical practice\r\n•\tOnline teaching experience\r\n•\tSuccessful faculty mentoring and development\r\n•\tExperience with graduate nursing accreditation processes Salary range: $154,306-$211,293 The position will remain open until filled. UMass Chan Medical School is committed to being an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer and recognizes the power of a diverse community. We encourage applications from protected veterans, individuals with disabilities, and those with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds to consider UMass Chan Medical School as their employer of choice. In alignment with our commitment to pay transparency, the base salary range for this\r\nposition is listed above (exclusive of benefits and retirement). At UMass Chan Medical School, final base salary offers are determined based on a\r\ncombination of factors, including your skills, education, and relevant experience. We also\r\nconsider internal equity to ensure fair and consistent compensation across our teams. Please note that the range provided reflects the full base salary range for this position.\r\nOffers are typically made within the starting range to allow for future growth and\r\ndevelopment within the role. In addition to base pay, UMass Chan offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package,\r\nwhich includes paid time off, medical, dental, and vision coverage, and participation in a\r\n401A retirement plan. As an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, UMass Chan recognizes the added value of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the  description. Further Info: 55 Lake Ave North Worcester, MA  01655 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    }
